Serve BeeZip's tools over MCP on stdin/stdout.

Commands that write files may only write under the --root directories (or `[mcp] roots` in
config.toml). Without either, MCP clients can read archives but not write anything. See docs/MCP.md.

Usage: beezip mcp [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --root <DIR>
          A directory commands may write under; repeatable. Replaces `[mcp] roots`

      --read-only
          Offer only the commands that don't write

      --unrestricted
          Let commands write anywhere

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Global options:
      --output <FORMAT>
          How to print results; ndjson streams every job event

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   One JSON document on stdout: the output, or `{"error": {...}}`
          - ndjson: Every job event as a JSON line on stdout, ending with `Finished`, `Failed` or
            `Cancelled`
          
          [default: human]

  -q, --quiet
          No progress bars or info messages; warnings still print
